{"choices":[{"message":{"content":"{\n  \"source_routes\": [\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0421\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The impact of sarcopenia on the efficacy and safety of immune checkpoint inhibitors in patients with solid tumours\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究提供肌肉量这一非微生物宿主因素对 ICI 疗效影响的实证数据，显示低肌肉量在肺癌中未降低 PFS 且不增加毒性。可用于 Ch1 作为对比背景，说明除微生物外其他宿主因素（如身体成分）的预测价值存在异质性，帮助界定微生物效应的独立性及临床解释的复杂性，避免将所有宿主预后因素一概而论。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0422\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut Associated Metabolites Enhance PD-L1 Blockade Efficacy in Prostate Cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究在前列腺癌模型中发现特定花生四烯酸代谢物（16(R)-HETE, 6-Keto-PGE1）通过上调外泌体 PD-L1 增强抗 PD-L1 疗效。可用于 Ch3 阐述代谢物介导机制的特异性案例，补充 Ch2 关于非经典免疫检查点调控路径的讨论。需注意其机制依赖于特定代谢环境且菌株未鉴定，体现代谢轴的情境依赖性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0423\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Targeting molecular pathways to control immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicities\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch6\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述将微生物组因素与特定细胞因子（IL-6, IL-17）及整合素通路联系起来，构建了微生物介导 irAEs 的分子机制框架。可用于 Ch6 解释微生物组如何通过系统性炎症反应影响免疫毒性，进而间接关联疗效 - 毒性平衡。需明确其侧重于毒性机制而非直接增效，作为理解微生物组双重作用的背景素材。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0424\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiota and metabolites associate with outcomes of immune checkpoint inhibitor–treated unresectable hepatocellular carcinoma\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch3\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究在 HCC 队列中识别出 Lachnoclostridium 富集与次级胆汁酸（UDCA/UCA）水平升高共同预测 ICI 疗效，提出“微生物 - 胆汁酸轴”假说。可用于 Ch1 提供肝癌特异性的微生物标志物证据，并用于 Ch3 阐述胆汁酸作为关键代谢中介的潜在机制。需注意其相关性性质及人群特异性（病毒相关 HCC）。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0425\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbial dysbiosis and childhood asthma development: Integrated role of the airway and gut microbiome, environmental exposures, and host metabolic and immune response\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述详细描述了肠道菌群代谢物（SCFAs）通过抑制 NF-κB、促进 Tregs 分化调节免疫稳态的机制，虽基于哮喘模型，但提供了通用的“微生物 - 代谢 - 免疫”通路框架。可用于 Ch2 作为背景理论支持，解释微生物代谢物系统性调节适应性免疫的生物学基础，类比其在肿瘤免疫中的潜在作用，需注明疾病模型差异。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0426\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"1038P Impact of metastatic location on immune-checkpoint inhibitors efficacy in patients with different solid tumours\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现转移灶数量（≥3 个）显著降低 ICI 疗效，但单发转移部位类型无影响。可用于 Ch1 作为临床预后基线数据，说明解剖学微环境差异未必决定疗效，从而凸显系统性因素（如肠道微生物组）在解释疗效异质性中的重要性。需注意其未涉及微生物数据，仅作为排除性或对照性临床变量参考。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0427\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Abstract 2377: Gut microbiome modulation by a black raspberry nectar for improving anti-PD1 therapy effectiveness in pre-clinical cancer models\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4\",\n        \"Ch3\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该摘要报道黑树莓花蜜通过增加 Lachnospiraceae/Blautia 及 L-肉碱水平增强小鼠抗 PD-1 疗效。可用于 Ch4 作为饮食干预调节微生物组进而影响 ICI 疗效的临床前案例，并用于 Ch3 提出 L-肉碱作为潜在新型代谢标志物的假设。需注意其仅为动物模型且 L-肉碱机制尚属相关性推测。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0428\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Comparison of baseline gut microbiome features between response subgroups of patients (pts) with advanced melanoma undergoing immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) therapy.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch6\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现黑色素瘤响应者中 SCFA 产生菌（如 F. prausnitzii）丰度更高，且高丰度菌群与无 irAEs 相关，挑战了\"irAEs 预示疗效”的直觉。可用于 Ch1 提供特定功能菌群与疗效关联的实证，并用于 Ch6 探讨微生物组在平衡疗效与毒性中的复杂角色，提示 SCFA 可能具有双重调节作用。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0429\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Enfortumab vedotin following platinum-based chemotherapy and immune checkpoint inhibitors for advanced urothelial carcinoma: response, survival and safety analysis from a multicentre real-world Japanese cohort.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究聚焦于 ICI 失败后尿路上皮癌患者使用抗体偶联药物（EV）的疗效与安全性，未涉及肠道微生物组数据或机制。虽提供实体瘤二线治疗背景，但与本综述核心问题（微生物调节 ICI 疗效及机制）无直接关联，故不纳入正文实质分析章节。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0430\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbiome bacterial influencers of host immunity and response to immunotherapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch5\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述系统总结了不同癌种中与 ICI 疗效相关的细菌类群（如 Ruminococcaceae, Akkermansiaceae）及其免疫调节机制（TLR 激活、代谢物调节 T 细胞）。可用于 Ch1/Ch2 提供跨癌种的微生物特征与机制汇总，Ch5 评估 FMT/益生菌现状，Ch7 指出异质性来源及标准化需求。需注意区分观察性关联与因果机制。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0431\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"β-catenin in dendritic cells negatively regulates CD8 T cell immune responses through the immune checkpoint molecule Tim-3 4802\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究阐明 DC 内β-catenin 信号通过上调 Tim-3 抑制 CD8+ T 细胞反应的机制，虽未直接涉及微生物，但揭示了免疫检查点分子在抗原呈递细胞层面的调控新路径。可用于 Ch2 作为宿主免疫内在调节机制的背景，补充说明除微生物外，DC 功能状态也是影响 ICI 疗效的关键因素，丰富机制讨论维度。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0432\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The gut microbiome affects response of treatments in HER2‐negative advanced gastric cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch3\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现胃癌中 Lactobacillus 丰度与 ICI 疗效正相关，且联合治疗具有独特的微生物组特征（非简单叠加）。可用于 Ch1 提供胃癌特异性微生物标志物证据，强调治疗情境依赖性；用于 Ch3 提供代谢通路差异（氨基酸/能量代谢富集）的线索。需注意其机制多为推测，且限于 HER2 阴性胃癌。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0433\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The relationship between gut microbiota and cancer immune response and immunotherapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\",\n        \"Ch5\",\n        \"Ch6\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述全面整合了微生物组与 ICI 疗效的临床关联、具体机制（SCFAs, TMAO, 色氨酸代谢）、干预策略（FMT, 益生菌）及毒性管理证据。可用于全篇各章提供核心机制细节、跨癌种比较数据及转化挑战分析。需注意其涵盖多种实体瘤，引用时需区分癌种特异性及证据等级（动物 vs 人类）。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0434\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Abstract PS2-07-12: Gut microbiome composition predicts pathologic complete response in patients with early-stage HER2-positive breast cancer receiving neoadjuvant HER2-targeted therapy +/- immunotherapy with pembrolizumab\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch6\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该摘要发现 HER2+ 乳腺癌新辅助治疗中，特定微生物特征预测含 ICI 方案的 pCR，且腹泻与微生物多样性相关。可用于 Ch1 提供乳腺癌新辅助场景下的微生物预测证据，强调治疗背景特异性；用于 Ch6 关联微生物组与 irAEs（腹泻）。需注意样本量小且菌种分类分辨率低，结果待验证。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0435\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"A comprehensive review of mechanisms underlying resistance to immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述详细阐述了微生物组通过调节髓系细胞、T 细胞激活及代谢产物（丁酸盐）影响 ICI 耐药的机制，并列出了有益/有害菌种。可用于 Ch1/Ch2 提供耐药背景下的微生物证据及具体分子通路（TLR, IL-12），Ch7 讨论异质性及因果推断局限。需注意区分肿瘤内在机制与微生物介导机制。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0436\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Abstract 6699: Delineating germline, tumor and extrinsic factors driving mucosal melanoma (MM) risk and response to immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) treatment\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该摘要描述了黏膜黑色素瘤队列中肠道与局部微生物组同步采集及多组学分析的研究设计，虽无结果数据，但提供了方法学范例。可用于 Ch7 讨论罕见肿瘤亚型的研究挑战、空间微生物组整合策略及未来多组学方向。需明确其仅为研究方案，不提供疗效关联结论。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0437\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gene-level gut microbiome signatures as predictive biomarkers for response to immune checkpoint inhibitors across multiple cancer types\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch3\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现基因水平微生物特征（如 nitrilase 基因）比分类学特征更能预测 CICB 疗效，且受年龄和治疗策略影响。可用于 Ch1 论证功能基因层面的预测优势，Ch3 提供氮代谢等潜在机制线索，Ch7 强调生物标志物的情境依赖性（治疗类型、年龄）。需注意其泛化性限于 CICB 背景。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0438\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gastrointestinal cancer resistance to treatment: the role of microbiota\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch4\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述聚焦消化道肿瘤，详述微生物通过代谢物（SCFAs, 胆汁酸）及免疫细胞训练（T 细胞多样性、MDSC 招募）调节治疗反应的机制，并提及抗生素/饮食影响。可用于 Ch2 提供 GI 癌特异性机制细节（如 F. nucleatum 抑制 NK），Ch4 讨论外部因素干扰。需注意其机制多基于临床前模型。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Harnessing the gut microbiome for improved immune checkpoint inhibition in colorectal cancer immunotherapy: a narrative Review.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\",\n        \"Ch5\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述针对结直肠癌（特别是 MSS/pMMR 亚型），总结了特定菌种（Akkermansia, Fusobacterium）与 ICI 疗效的关联、代谢及免疫机制（TLR4, SCFAs）及干预策略。可用于 Ch1-Ch5 提供 CRC 特异性证据及机制框架，Ch7 指出矛盾发现（如 A. muciniphila 的双重作用）及安全挑战。需注意其叙事性综述性质。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0440\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"An observational study to evaluate pattern of usage of immune checkpoint inhibitors in the 1st line treatment of various advanced solid tumors, their efficacy and their toxicity profile.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究提供真实世界中 ICI 一线治疗的总体疗效（ORR 31.25%）及毒性谱（肺炎、皮疹高发）基线数据。可用于 Ch1 作为临床背景参考，帮助读者理解 ICI 在广泛实体瘤中的实际表现，作为评估微生物组等特定因素效应大小的基准。需注意其未涉及微生物数据，仅提供宏观临床概况。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0441\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) as \\\"chemotherapy (Ctx) sensitization\\\" strategy in advanced solid tumours\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现 ICI 序贯化疗在难治性实体瘤中未显示优于靶向药序贯化疗的获益，提示 ICI 的“致敏”效应非普遍存在。可用于 Ch1 作为阴性结果案例，说明若无特定修饰因子（如特定微生物组），ICI 未必能改善后续治疗疗效，从而反衬微生物组作为关键调节因子的潜在重要性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0442\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The microbiome and gynaecological cancer development, prevention and therapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch5\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述片段提及口服 A. muciniphila 可恢复小鼠对 PD-1 抑制剂的响应，并涉及双歧杆菌的免疫调节作用。可用于 Ch2 提供特定菌株增强 ICI 疗效的临床前机制证据，Ch5 讨论 FMT/益生菌策略。需注意其主要语境为妇科癌症，且机制多基于动物模型，外推需谨慎。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0443\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Non-small cell lung cancer patients treated with Anti-PD1 immunotherapy show distinct microbial signatures and metabolic pathways according to progression-free survival and PD-L1 status\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch3\",\n        \"Ch4\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究在 NSCLC 中识别出 Alistipes（有益）和 Streptococcus（有害）与 PFS 的物种水平关联，并发现化疗虽改变菌群但不消除预测信号。可用于 Ch1 提供稳健的物种级标志物，Ch3 提供代谢通路（氨基酸合成）线索，Ch4 讨论化疗预处理对微生物组的影响及独立性。需注意其限于高加索人群。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0444\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbial metabolic pathways guide response to immune checkpoint blockade therapy.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究提出“功能性菌群失调”概念，阐明 MEP 通路（HMBPP 激活 Vδ2 T 细胞）促免疫与核黄素通路（5-OP-RU 激活 MAIT 细胞）抑免疫的双向机制。可用于 Ch2/Ch3 深入解析代谢通路特异性调控人类特有 T 细胞亚群的分子机制，强调功能而非物种组成的重要性。需注意其机制验证主要在体外/PDTO 模型。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0445\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The future of affordable cancer immunotherapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch5\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述讨论微生物组疗法（如 FMT）作为低成本增强 ICI 疗效策略的潜力，提及 SCFA 及细菌组成的预测价值。可用于 Ch5 从卫生经济学角度论证微生物干预的可及性优势，提供非侵入性监测（粪便 SCFA）及低成本干预的背景。需注意其侧重成本而非深度机制，证据多为早期观察。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0446\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Multi-omics analysis of saccharomyces boulardii supplementation reveals coordinated microbiome, metabolic, and immune signaling changes accompanying tumor suppression\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\",\n        \"Ch5\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现益生菌 S. boulardii 通过产生/促进 AhR 配体（5-HIAA, IPA）抑制结直肠癌生长，并降低 CTLA-4 等因子。可用于 Ch2/Ch3 阐述色氨酸代谢-AhR 轴介导的免疫调节机制，Ch5 作为标准化益生菌替代 FMT 的可行性案例。需注意其为皮下移植瘤模型，且 IPA 来源为间接推断。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0447\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbial metabolites and their influence on the tumor microenvironment\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述详述 SCFAs、胆汁酸、色氨酸代谢物通过重塑免疫细胞代谢（糖酵解、FAO）及信号通路（AhR, GPCR）调节 TME 的机制。可用于 Ch2/Ch3 提供代谢重编程在微生物 - 免疫互作中的核心地位证据，解释代谢物如何作为关键信使影响 ICI 疗效。需注意其涵盖多种代谢物，引用时需区分具体通路及癌症类型。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0448\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Role of gut microbiome in the outcome of lymphoma patients treated with checkpoint inhibitors—The MicroLinf Study\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究聚焦淋巴瘤（血液系统恶性肿瘤），发现 Lachnospira 与响应相关。因本综述限定于实体瘤，且淋巴瘤微环境与实体瘤差异显著，该材料不宜作为实体瘤微生物调节机制的直接证据，仅可作为极边缘的对比案例，故不纳入正文实质分析章节以避免混淆。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0449\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut Microbiota Metabolites and Chronic Diseases: Interactions, Mechanisms, and Therapeutic Strategies\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述详述 SCFAs、胆汁酸在慢性病中调节免疫细胞（巨噬细胞、T 细胞）及炎症通路（NF-κB）的机制。可用于 Ch2 作为背景知识，提供微生物代谢物调节宿主免疫的通用生物学原理，支持其在肿瘤免疫中作用的合理性假设。需注意其非肿瘤特异性，机制需结合肿瘤语境谨慎外推。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0450\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut Microbiota and Response to Immunotherapeutic Drugs in Oncology: More Questions Than Answers\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述汇总了早期研究中与 ICI 疗效相关的菌种列表及不一致性，指出机制空白及转化障碍（监管、标准化）。可用于 Ch1 列举早期观察性证据，Ch7 强调领域局限性、异质性来源及未来标准化需求。需注意其发表于 2020 年，代表早期认知状态，需结合最新研究更新观点。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0451\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Harnessing the Gut Microbiome in Cancer Immunotherapy: Mechanisms, Challenges, and Routes to Personalized Medicine—A Systematic Review\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\",\n        \"Ch5\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该系统综述总结了特定菌株（Akkermansia, Faecalibacterium）及代谢物（SCFAs, I3A）调节免疫的机制，评估了 FMT/益生菌临床证据及个性化医疗挑战。可用于全篇提供机制细节、干预策略现状及未来方向。需注意其涵盖临床前与临床数据，引用时需区分证据等级及人群差异。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0452\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Sucralose and the Gut–Immune Axis: Emerging Evidence Linking Dysbiosis, Barrier Alterations, and Implications for Colitis and Colorectal Cancer Immunotherapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4\",\n        \"Ch3\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述提出三氯蔗糖通过减少产丁酸菌、降低精氨酸/瓜氨酸水平抑制 CD8+ T 细胞功能从而削弱 ICI 疗效的机制。可用于 Ch4 作为饮食负面调节因子的具体案例，Ch3 阐述精氨酸代谢途径介导的免疫抑制机制。需注意其人类证据有限，主要基于动物模型及观察性关联。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0453\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Effect of dual immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) by the time of infusion in advanced non–small cell lung cancer (NSCLC): A secondary analysis of CCTG BR34 trial.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现双 ICI 方案下午输注优于上午，提示时间生物学效应具有方案特异性。可用于 Ch4 讨论宿主节律（非微生物直接因素）作为外部调节变量的复杂性，说明疗效调节因素的多维性。需注意其未涉及微生物机制，仅作为宿主生理因素干扰疗效的背景参考。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0454\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Eating away cancer: the potential of diet and the microbiome for shaping immunotherapy outcome\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4\",\n        \"Ch3\",\n        \"Ch2\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述系统梳理了饮食模式（高纤维、生酮等）通过重塑微生物组及代谢物（SCFAs, 胆汁酸）影响 ICI 疗效的机制与临床证据。可用于 Ch4 评估饮食干预策略，Ch2/Ch3 提供饮食 - 微生物 - 免疫轴的具体代谢及细胞机制。需注意其证据多为观察性或临床前，需区分商业益生菌与天然来源。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0455\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiome in gastrointestinal neoplasms: from mechanisms to precision therapeutic strategies\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\",\n        \"Ch5\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述聚焦 GI 肿瘤，详述微生物通过免疫重塑（AhR/IDO1, CXCR3+ T 细胞）及代谢移位调节 ICI 疗效的机制，评估 FMT/工程菌策略。可用于 Ch1-Ch3 提供 GI 癌特异性机制及标志物，Ch5 讨论精准治疗策略。需注意其机制多基于临床前或早期试验，需强调肿瘤类型特异性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0456\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The Resistance Mechanisms of Checkpoint Inhibitors in Solid Tumors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述将微生物群列为 ICI 耐药六大机制之一，详述其通过交叉反应、DC 激活等途径调节疗效，并对比其他耐药机制。可用于 Ch1/Ch2 提供耐药背景下的微生物证据及机制分类框架，Ch7 讨论多因素交互作用。需注意其发表于 2020 年，部分机制需结合最新研究更新。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0457\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The tumor microbiome and cancer immunotherapy: A systematic review of a new frontier beyond the gut.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述聚焦肿瘤内微生物群（非肠道），阐述其通过局部免疫调节（Th1 极化、Treg 募集）影响 ICI 疗效的机制。可用于 Ch2 作为肠道菌群全身效应之外的局部机制补充，丰富对微生物 - 免疫互作空间维度的理解。需明确区分作用部位（局部 vs 全身），避免混淆概念。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0458\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Examining the impact of the microbiome on cancer immunotherapy outcomes: A review\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch5\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述概括了有益菌（Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium）与 ICI 疗效的关联及三大机制路径（代谢物、细胞因子、抗原呈递），并讨论干预挑战。可用于 Ch1/Ch2 提供宏观概念框架及机制分类，Ch5 简述转化障碍。需注意其为高层级综述，缺乏具体数据细节，适合作为背景引入。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0459\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The circadian-microbiome-immune axis in colorectal cancer: mechanisms of spatiotemporal immunosuppression and chronotherapeutic horizons\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch4\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述提出“时间性免疫抑制”框架，阐述昼夜节律紊乱通过微生物代谢物（TCA）及 MDSCs 时相性积累抑制 ICI 疗效的机制。可用于 Ch2 提供时间生物学维度的机制假说，Ch4 讨论节律作为外部干扰因素及时间治疗学潜力。需注意其基于小鼠模型，人类验证尚缺。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0460\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Therapeutic targeting of the host-microbiota-immune axis: implications for precision health\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch5\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述详述厚壁菌门成员（F. prausnitzii）通过代谢物（丁酸盐）、抗原呈递及屏障功能调节 ICI 疗效的机制，并提及 FMT 证据。可用于 Ch1/Ch2 提供具体菌属及多重机制解释，Ch5 讨论干预策略。需注意其机制多基于动物模型，需区分观察关联与因果链条。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0461\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Immune checkpoint inhibitors in melanoma: mechanisms, immune cell interactions, and the tumour microenvironment\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述聚焦皮肤微生物组及 TME 一般机制，未涉及肠道微生物组对 ICI 疗效的调节。因本综述核心为肠道微生物轴，皮肤微生物机制虽相关但属不同生态位，直接纳入易致混淆，故不作为正文实质分析材料，仅在极必要时作为解剖特异性对比提及。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0462\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiome metabolites, molecular mimicry, and species-level variation drive long-term efficacy and adverse event outcomes in lung cancer survivors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\",\n        \"Ch6\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究从代谢物（SCFAs）、分子模拟（抗原交叉反应）及菌株变异三维度解析微生物调节 ICI 疗效及 irAEs 的机制。可用于 Ch1/Ch3 提供长期获益的代谢标志物，Ch2 阐述分子模拟机制，Ch6 关联 irAEs。需注意分子模拟为生物信息学预测，需结合功能验证解读。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0463\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The Great Debate at'Immunotherapy Bridge', Naples, December 5, 2019\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch4\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该辩论报告呈现了微生物组成 vs 饮食功能在调节 ICI 疗效中的不同视角，指出缺乏跨队列一致菌种。可用于 Ch4 引入饮食干预的潜在角色，Ch7 讨论“功能优于组成”的观点及研究异质性挑战。需注意其为专家观点汇总，非实证数据，适合作为争议点背景。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0464\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Potential mechanisms and targeting strategies of the gut microbiota in antitumor immunity and immunotherapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\",\n        \"Ch5\",\n        \"Ch6\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述详尽阐述了微生物通过 MAMPs、代谢物（SCFAs, 肌苷）、分子模拟及屏障功能调节 ICI 疗效的四大机制，并总结干预策略。可用于全篇提供核心机制细节、菌株案例及转化现状。需注意其基于大量临床前数据，引用时需明确人体验证程度及癌种差异。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0465\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Development of a novel immune-related toxicity grading system for predicting outcomes in patients with solid tumours treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI).\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch6\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现 irAEs 的多器官受累特征比单一毒性更能预测生存获益，提供“毒性 - 疗效”正相关的临床证据。可用于 Ch6 支持 irAEs 作为疗效预测因子的观点，提示系统性免疫激活的重要性。需注意其未涉及微生物机制，仅作为临床现象背景，机制解释需结合其他研究。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0466\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Shaping the Future of Immunotherapy Targets and Biomarkers in Melanoma and Non-Melanoma Cutaneous Cancers\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch5\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述总结黑色素瘤中微生物组成（双歧杆菌、Ruminococcaceae）与 ICI 疗效的关联及 FMT 恢复响应的证据，提出代谢及抗原交叉反应机制。可用于 Ch1/Ch2 提供皮肤癌特异性数据及机制假说，Ch5 评估 FMT 潜力。需注意其机制多基于早期临床或临床前数据，外推需谨慎。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0467\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Managing Resistance to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors in Lung Cancer: Treatment and Novel Strategies.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该摘要聚焦肺癌 ICI 耐药的通用机制及治疗策略，未提及肠道微生物组的具体作用或数据。虽提供耐药背景框架，但缺乏与本综述核心问题（微生物调节机制）的直接关联，无法提供实质性分析素材，故不纳入正文章节。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0468\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"From Womb to World: Unravelling the Microbiota′s Impact on Health and Disease\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch5\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述汇总微生物多样性、特定菌属（Bacteroides）与 ICI 疗效的关联及 FMT 证据，讨论方法学挑战。可用于 Ch1/Ch2 提供基础关联及机制线索（T 细胞激活），Ch5 介绍 FMT 转化进展，Ch7 指出方法学异质性。需注意其为叙事性综述，证据等级需结合原始研究判断。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0469\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiota-mediated immunomodulation in tumor\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch4\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述全面总结特定微生物特征（Ruminococcaceae, Akkermansia）与 ICI 疗效的关联，详述 PAMPs 及代谢物（丁酸盐）介导的免疫调节机制，并讨论抗生素干扰。可用于 Ch1/Ch2 提供核心证据及机制框架，Ch4 评估外部因素，Ch7 指出异质性来源。需注意其涵盖多癌种，引用时需区分情境。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0470\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The impact of gut microbiota modulation on responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors in cancer.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch5\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该荟萃分析汇总了特定菌属（Akkermansia 等）富集、抗生素暴露及 FMT 对 ICI 疗效的定量效应量。可用于 Ch1 提供群体水平的统计关联证据，Ch5 支持干预策略的有效性。需注意其为荟萃分析结果，反映统计关联而非个体因果机制，且未分层具体癌种。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0471\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut Microbiota and Cancer: From Pathogenesis to Therapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch5\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述汇总早期关键研究，指出响应者富集 Akkermansia/Bifidobacterium 及抗生素负面影响，阐述 TNF 产生、T 细胞浸润等机制。可用于 Ch1/Ch2 提供里程碑式证据及基础机制解释，Ch5 讨论益生菌/FMT 现状。需注意其发表于 2019 年，部分观点需结合最新研究更新。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0472\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Immunometabolism: The role of gut‐derived microbial metabolites in optimising immune response during checkpoint inhibitor therapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\",\n        \"Ch6\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述详述 SCFA 促进 CD8+ T 细胞功能、色氨酸代谢抑制免疫的具体分子机制，并讨论益生菌干预的复杂性。可用于 Ch2/Ch3 提供代谢重编程及信号通路细节，Ch6 关联代谢物与 irAEs。需注意其引用研究样本量小，且动物模型结果需谨慎外推至人类。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0473\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Abstract 6687: Evaluation of a new co-cultured microbiome ecosystem therapy candidate (MaaT034) for clinical testing as adjuvant/neoadjuvant to immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\",\n        \"Ch5\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该摘要介绍共培养微生物组疗法 MaaT034 通过分泌 SCFAs/次级胆汁酸、修复屏障及促进 DC-T 细胞互作增强 ICI 敏感性的体外机制。可用于 Ch2/Ch3 提供标准化微生物制剂的作用机制案例，Ch5 展示从 FMT 向工业化产品演进的技术路线。需注意其仅为体外数据，临床效果待验证。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Tumor microenvironment-mediated resistance to immune checkpoint inhibitors in non-small cell lung cancer: Mechanisms, combination strategies and clinical perspectives (Review)\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述提及 NSCLC 中 Akkermansia/Bifidobacterium 的潜在益处及 Fusobacterium 的谨慎外推，强调系统性因素（含微生物组）与 TME 的交互。可用于 Ch1 提供肺癌特异性微生物背景，Ch7 讨论疾病特异性验证需求及干预局限性。需注意其机制描述概括，需结合其他研究细化。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0475\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Exploring Gut–Brain Interaction Disorders: Mechanisms and Translational Therapies Crossing Neurology to Gastroenterology\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述聚焦肠 - 脑轴及神经胃肠疾病，虽提及微生物组一般机制，但未涉及实体瘤或 ICI 疗效的具体数据或机制。其内容与本综述核心主题（肿瘤免疫治疗）距离较远，无法提供实质性分析素材，故不纳入正文章节。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0476\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut metabolites: key factors in the cross-talk between the gut microbiota and tumor immunotherapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述详述代谢物（TMAO, SCFAs, LPS）在不同肿瘤中双向调节 ICI 疗效的机制（受体信号、细胞分化），强调情境依赖性。可用于 Ch2/Ch3 深入解析代谢物效应的异质性及具体分子路径（AhR, FXR 等）。需注意其机制多基于临床前研究，引用时需明确肿瘤类型及微环境条件。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0477\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Targeting the gut microbiota-metabolite-immune axis in cancer immunotherapy: mechanistic interplay, therapeutic strategies, and translational applications-a narrative review\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\",\n        \"Ch5\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述系统总结跨癌种微生物特征、核心代谢物（丁酸盐、肌苷、胆汁酸）的双向机制及干预策略转化现状。可用于全篇提供机制框架、癌种特异性标志物及未来方向。需注意其为叙事性综述，证据等级不一，引用时需区分观察关联与因果验证程度。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0478\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Cross-cohort gut microbiome associations with immune checkpoint inhibitor response in advanced melanoma\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch1\",\n        \"Ch7\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究揭示黑色素瘤中微生物标志物的跨队列异质性，指出无通用生物标志物，但部分菌种（Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia）具一致性。可用于 Ch1 提供重复性较高的候选菌种，Ch7 强调方法学挑战（批次效应、队列偏差）及生物标志物开发的复杂性。需注意其结论限于黑色素瘤。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0479\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut Metabolites and Breast Cancer: The Continuum of Dysbiosis, Breast Cancer Risk, and Potential Breast Cancer Therapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"Ch2\",\n        \"Ch3\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述详述 SCFAs（丁酸盐）作为 HDAC 抑制剂及肌苷调节 TH1 分化的机制，虽主要基于其他实体瘤数据，但提供了代谢物调节免疫的通用原理。可用于 Ch2/Ch3 作为机制背景支持，解释代谢物在乳腺癌及其他实体瘤中潜在的免疫调节作用。需注意其乳腺癌特异性临床数据有限。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0480\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"A prospective translational study investigating the association of gut microbiome (GM) diversity with pathological complete response (pCR) after neoadjuvant treatment in early stage rectal and esophageal cancers.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该摘要仅为研究方案，无结果数据，且聚焦于新辅助放化疗而非 ICI 治疗。虽涉及微生物多样性与治疗反应关联的假设，但缺乏针对 ICI 疗效的实质证据或机制分析，无法支撑本综述核心论点，故不纳入正文实质分析章节。\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"The user wants me to route a batch of 60 sources (P0421 to P0480) to the chapters of a review outline about how the gut microbiome modulates immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) efficacy in solid tumors.\n\nI need to:\n1. Read each source's B planning card carefully\n2. Determine which chapter(s) each source belongs to based on its actual content (not just title/claims)\n3. Write 80-150 Chinese characters explaining the specific usable material for each routed source\n4. Return JSON only with source_routes array\n\nLet me analyze each source:\n\nP0421: Sarcopenia impact on ICI efficacy - NOT about gut microbiome. This is about body composition (muscle mass). Should be routed to chapters discussing non-microbiome host factors or excluded. Looking at the chapters, none specifically cover non-microbiome host factors. This might be marginally relevant for Ch7 (methodological challenges/confounders) or Ch1 (clinical associations - as a contrast). Actually, the planning card says it's not directly related to gut microbiome. I should route it carefully - maybe Ch1 as a contrast example of non-microbiome factors, or exclude it. Given the instruction to route every input, I'll put it in Ch1 with a note that it's a non-microbiome host factor for contrast.\n\nP0422: Gut metabolites (16(R)-HETE, 6-Keto-PGE1) enhancing PD-L1 blockade in prostate cancer - This is about metabolites mediating ICI efficacy. Fits Ch3 (metabolites) and Ch2 (mechanisms).\n\nP0423: Targeting molecular pathways to control ICI toxicities - Abstract only, focuses on irAEs mechanisms. Fits Ch6 (toxicity) and Ch2 (mechanisms).\n\nP0424: Gut microbiota and metabolites in HCC patients on ICI - Clinical evidence in HCC. Fits Ch1 (clinical associations) and Ch3 (metabolites - bile acids).\n\n\nP0425: Microbial dysbiosis and childhood asthma - NOT about cancer/ICI. This is about asthma. Should be excluded or routed to Ch2 as background mechanism (SCFAs regulating immunity) with clear caveats. The planning card notes it's not about tumors or ICIs. I'll route to Ch2 with clear limitations noted.\n\nP0426: Metastatic location impact on ICI efficacy - Abstract only, not about microbiome. This is about clinical factors. Similar to P0421, could be Ch1 as non-microbiome factor contrast.\n\nP0427: Black raspberry nectar modulating microbiome for anti-PD1 in preclinical models - Diet intervention affecting microbiome and ICI response. Fits Ch4 (external factors/diet) and Ch5 (intervention strategies).\n\nP0428: Baseline gut microbiome in melanoma ICI patients - Clinical association study. Fits Ch1 (clinical associations) and Ch6 (irAEs association).\n\nP0429: Enfortumab vedotin after ICI in urothelial carcinoma - NOT about microbiome. This is about ADC therapy after ICI failure. Should be excluded or minimal routing. Planning card says no microbiome data. I'll route to Ch1 as post-ICI treatment context with clear note.\n\nP0430: Microbiome bacterial influencers review - Comprehensive review on mechanisms. Fits Ch2 (mechanisms), Ch3 (metabolites), Ch5 (interventions).\n\nP0431: β-catenin in DCs regulating Tim-3 - NOT about gut microbiome. This is about DC intrinsic signaling. Should be Ch2 as immune mechanism background with caveat.\n\nP0432: Gut microbiome in HER2-negative gastric cancer ICI - Clinical evidence in gastric cancer. Fits Ch1 (clinical associations) and Ch2 (mechanisms).\n\nP0433: Gut microbiota and cancer immune response review - Comprehensive review. Fits Ch2 (mechanisms), Ch3 (metabolites), Ch5 (interventions), Ch6 (toxicity).\n\nP0434: Gut microbiome predicting pCR in HER2+ breast cancer neoadjuvant therapy - Abstract only, breast cancer with ICI + targeted therapy. Fits Ch1 (clinical associations).\n\nP0435: Review of ICI resistance mechanisms - Includes microbiome section. Fits Ch2 (mechanisms), Ch1 (clinical associations).\n\nP0436: Mucosal melanoma microbiome study protocol - Abstract only, protocol not results. Fits Ch7 (methodological considerations).\n\nP0437: Gene-level microbiome signatures predicting ICI response across cancers - Multi-cancer analysis. Fits Ch1 (clinical associations), Ch2 (mechanisms - metabolic pathways), Ch7 (methodological).\n\nP0438: GI cancer resistance and microbiota review - Focus on GI cancers. Fits Ch1 (clinical associations), Ch2 (mechanisms).\n\nP0439: Gut microbiome in CRC immunotherapy review - CRC-specific. Fits Ch1, Ch2, Ch3, Ch5.\n\nP0440: Observational study on ICI usage patterns and toxicity - NOT about microbiome. General ICI safety/efficacy data. Fits Ch6 (toxicity baseline) with caveat.\n\nP0441: ICI as chemotherapy sensitization - Abstract only, not about microbiome. Fits Ch1 as treatment context.\n\nP0442: Microbiome and gynaecological cancer - Review including FMT evidence. Fits Ch2, Ch5.\n\nP0443: NSCLC patients on anti-PD1 with microbial signatures - Clinical evidence in lung cancer. Fits Ch1, Ch2, Ch3 (metabolic pathways).\n\nP0444: Microbial metabolic pathways guiding ICB response - Mechanistic focus on MEP and riboflavin pathways. Fits Ch2, Ch3.\n\nP0445: Affordable cancer immunotherapy review - Includes microbiome as low-cost option. Fits Ch5 (interventions).\n\nP0446: S. boulardii supplementation multi-omics - Preclinical mechanistic study. Fits Ch2, Ch3 (metabolites - AhR ligands).\n\nP0447: Microbial metabolites and TME review - Comprehensive metabolite review. Fits Ch2, Ch3.\n\nP0448: Microbiome in lymphoma ICI - Abstract only, lymphoma (not solid tumor). Fits Ch1 with caveat about tumor type.\n\nP0449: Gut metabolites and chronic diseases review - NOT cancer-specific. General immunometabolism. Fits Ch3 as background mechanism.\n\nP0450: Gut microbiota and ICI response review (2020) - Early review highlighting knowledge gaps. Fits Ch2, Ch7.\n\nP0451: Harnessing gut microbiome in cancer immunotherapy systematic review - Comprehensive. Fits Ch2, Ch3, Ch5, Ch7.\n\nP0452: Sucralose and gut-immune axis in CRC immunotherapy - Diet component affecting microbiome and ICI. Fits Ch3, Ch4.\n\nP0453: Dual ICI infusion timing in NSCLC - Abstract only, chronotherapy not microbiome. Fits Ch4 (external factors - timing) with caveat.\n\nP0454: Diet and microbiome for immunotherapy outcome review - Diet-microbiome-ICI axis. Fits Ch3, Ch4, Ch5.\n\nP0455: Gut microbiome in GI neoplasms review - GI cancer focus. Fits Ch1, Ch2, Ch3, Ch5.\n\nP0456: ICI resistance mechanisms review (2020) - Includes microbiome section. Fits Ch2, Ch7.\n\nP0457: Tumor